  "$comment": "Public keys only, per cluster, written by scripts/chain/bootstrap.ts from what the chain holds after it runs, and by scripts/chain/deploy.ts on a deploy or an upgrade (programSha256: the verified sha256 of the bytes deployed; upgrade: a prepared buffer and its verified sha256, until the upgrade authority applies it). governance names who holds the roles: single-key (owner decision #541: the owner's key is the upgrade authority, the Config's admin and its arbiter, and a separate owner key is its guardian, none of them on the server; the upgrade authority moves only by SetAuthorityChecked, which the new key co-signs, so while a prepared handover waits upgradeAuthority is still the deploy key and roles.upgradeAuthority names the owner's), or squads (a test cluster: squads.vault is every escrow's arbiter, and upgradeAuthority is the deploy key). closed: the slot at which deploy.ts close read the program closed (its ProgramData and metadata gone, their rent returned; the program never runs again). Localnet addresses all derive from key files, so they survive a ledger reset.",
